## Stack

- React 19, TypeScript (strict), Vite. Node 24, pnpm (version pinned in `package.json` `packageManager`).
- TanStack Router (file routes in `src/routes`), TanStack Query, TanStack Table v8.
- Tailwind 4 and shadcn/ui (Radix) primitives in `src/components/ui`.
- react-hook-form with zod 4 resolvers.
- API client generated by `@hey-api/openapi-ts` from `openapi.json` into `src/client` (fetch client, TanStack Query options, zod schemas).
- Vitest, Testing Library, MSW 3.
- ESLint (with jsx-a11y) and Prettier.
- Static production image: nginx on port 8080 (`Dockerfile`, `nginx.conf`).

## Commands

Run from `frontend/`. Prefer the Makefile over raw tool calls.

- `make dev`: Vite dev server; `/api` is proxied to `API_PROXY_TARGET` (default `http://localhost:8000`).
- `make test`: Vitest, single run.
- `make lint`: ESLint plus Prettier check.
- `make fmt`: Prettier write plus ESLint fix.
- `make check`: lint, typecheck, test, build. The gate before every commit.
- `make gen-api`: regenerate `src/client` from `openapi.json`.

## Architecture map

- `openapi.json`: copy of the backend admin spec. Source of truth for `src/client`.
- `src/client/`: generated, never edited. `src/client-config.ts` sets base URL and `credentials: 'include'`.
- `src/main.tsx`, `src/router.tsx`: app entry and router factory (`createAppRouter`, `bindSessionExpiry`).
- `src/env.ts`: the only reader of `import.meta.env` (zod-parsed).
- `src/lib/auth.ts`: in-memory access token, refresh, login/logout, request and response interceptors.
- `src/lib/session.ts`: `ensureAdmin`, the route guard check. `src/lib/problem.ts`: `getProblem`, `showProblem`.
- `src/lib/query.ts`: `invalidateOp` for cache invalidation by operation id.
- `src/routes/`: `login.tsx`, layout `_app.tsx`, pages under `_app/` (`items`, `users`). `routeTree.gen.ts` is generated.
- `src/components/data-table/`: `data-table.tsx` (generic table) and `search.ts` (`makeListSearchSchema`, `toQuery`).
- `src/hooks/`: shared hooks (`use-mobile.ts`). `src/lib/redirect.ts`: `safeRedirect` for the login `redirect` param.
- `src/components/`: `items-table.tsx`, `users-table.tsx`, `item-form.tsx`, `login-form.tsx`, `ui/`.
- `.claude/`, `.mcp.json`: Claude Code skills, the reviewer subagent, MCP servers (see `CLAUDE.md`).
- `src/test/`: MSW `server.ts`, `handlers.ts`, `fixtures.ts`, `render.tsx` (`renderApp`), `setup.ts`.

Auth flow:

1. The access token lives in a module variable in `src/lib/auth.ts`; the refresh token is an httpOnly `SameSite=Strict` cookie.
2. The route guard in `src/routes/_app.tsx` calls `ensureAdmin` (`src/lib/session.ts`), which uses `ensureSession`; that refreshes once (single flight) when no token is held.
3. A 401 on a normal request triggers one refresh and one retry of that request.
4. A 401 from refresh clears the token and fires `onSessionExpired` (only if a token was held), which sends the user to `/login`. Other failures (network, 5xx) leave the session as it is.
5. `ensureAdmin` logs out any non-admin user.

Data flow: a route validates the URL search params (`makeListSearchSchema`), passes `search` and a stable `onSearchChange` to a table component, which calls the generated `*Options` with `toQuery(search)` and hands rows to `DataTable`.

## Conventions

- Generated names come from backend operationIds (`itemsListOptions`, `itemsUpdateMutation`, `zItemCreate`). Rename the operationId in the backend, not here.
- List pages: URL search params are the state. Build the schema with `makeListSearchSchema(allowedSort)`.
- Errors: read them with `getProblem`, show them with `showProblem`. Do not parse error bodies by hand.
- Forms use the generated zod schemas (`src/client/zod.gen.ts`), extended only when the UI needs more.
- Read env only through `src/env.ts`. Never touch `import.meta.env` elsewhere.
- Keep the access token in memory only (`src/lib/auth.ts`).
- Invalidate caches with `invalidateOp(qc, 'itemsList', ...)`. Never build query keys by hand.
- `@tanstack/react-table` is pinned to v8; use the v8 API only.
- `DataTable` `onSearchChange` must be a stable callback (wrap it in `useCallback`); its empty-last-page effect depends on it.
- Callers do not pass `defaultSort` to `DataTable`. Its header-click cycle reads `search.sort`, while `aria-sort` and the icon read `search.sort ?? defaultSort`, so the cycle would look inconsistent.
- `items-table.tsx` and `users-table.tsx` are the reference table components; copy their shape for a new resource.
- Mutations: pass `onError: showProblem` and invalidate the list and get operations in `onSuccess`.
- Import app code through the `@/` alias, not long relative paths.
- Interactive controls need accessible names (`aria-label`); ESLint jsx-a11y enforces the basics.

## Testing

- Vitest with Testing Library and MSW 3. Tests run against the real generated client; only the network is mocked.
- `src/test/setup.ts` starts the server with `onUnhandledFrame: 'error'`, so any request without a handler fails the test.
- Add handlers in `src/test/handlers.ts`; override per test with `server.use(...)`. Shared data lives in `src/test/fixtures.ts`.
- Render whole routes with `renderApp(path)` from `src/test/render.tsx`.
- Keep fixtures typed with the generated types so a spec change breaks the test at compile time.
- Query by role and name (`getByRole`, `findByRole`) first; fall back to labels, then text. Avoid test ids.
- Reset auth state between tests with `__resetAuthForTests` (already wired in `setup.ts`).
- Unit tests sit next to the code (`*.test.ts`, `*.test.tsx`).

## Deploy

Admin and API must be served from the same site (one reverse proxy routing `/api` to the backend and `/` to this app, or sibling subdomains of one registrable domain) because the refresh cookie is `SameSite=Strict`. The `Dockerfile` builds a static nginx image on port 8080 and does not proxy `/api`; a front proxy must.

## Definition of done

- `make check` is green.
- `make gen-api` leaves no diff in `src/client`.
- When the backend API changed, copy its `openapi/admin.json` over `openapi.json` first, then run `make gen-api`.
- New behaviour has a test.
- The Dockerfile still builds (`docker build -t {{ project_slug }}-admin .`) when dependencies or build config changed.

## Never

- Never edit `src/client/` or `src/routeTree.gen.ts` by hand.
- Never store tokens in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, cookies set from JS, or IndexedDB.
- Never hand-build query keys.
- Never read `import.meta.env` outside `src/env.ts`.
- Never break the same-site deploy: no cross-site API hosts, no `SameSite` relaxation.
